    "different_in_kind_from_code47": "In code/47 a bitwise-identical LEAKY/CLEAN_MATCHED pair meant both selection rules had saturated onto the last epoch, so the harness had no contrast to measure and the cell's near-zero gap was an artifact. Here it means the two honest selection rules picked the SAME INIT SEED out of K, whose chance rate is ~1/K. That is a real (and informative) property of exchangeable selection, not an instrumentation failure, so gating on it is reported but not privileged."
